@startuml
title Bloater: Large Class -- AFTER (Refactored)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #D4EDDA
skinparam ClassBorderColor #28A745
skinparam ClassFontSize 13
skinparam ClassAttributeFontSize 11

note "REFACTORED: Extract Class\nSingle Responsibility Principle" as N1 #69DB7C

class Order <<Clean Code>> {
  - customer : Customer
  - shippingAddress : ShippingAddress
  - billingAddress : BillingAddress
  - items : List<Item>
  - status : OrderStatus
  --
  + addItem(item : Item) : void
  + calculateTotal() : double
}

class Customer <<Clean Code>> {
  - name : String
  - email : String
  - phone : String
  --
  + updateProfile() : void
}

class ShippingAddress <<Clean Code>> {
  - street : String
  - city : String
  - state : String
  - zip : String
  --
  + format() : String
}

class BillingAddress <<Clean Code>> {
  - street : String
  - city : String
  - state : String
  - zip : String
  --
  + format() : String
}

class OrderShipper <<Clean Code>> {
  + shipOrder(order : Order) : void
  + sendConfirmation(order : Order) : void
}

Order --> Customer
Order --> ShippingAddress
Order --> BillingAddress
Order ..> OrderShipper : uses

N1 .. Order

note bottom of Order
  <color:#28A745><b>Benefits:</b></color>
  - Each class has ONE responsibility
  - Easier to test in isolation
  - Smaller classes are reusable
  - No code duplication
end note

@enduml
